WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.100
A configuration baseline represents an approved starting point or expected state for a system.

2
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:11.000
It describes how a system should be configured when it is operating within approved boundaries.

3
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:23.600
Baselines may define operating system settings, security controls, software versions, network configurations, logging settings, identity settings, and other approved parameters.

4
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.400
Baselines help organizations establish consistency.

5
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:36.140
When systems are built from a known reference, teams can troubleshoot faster, enforce expectations more clearly, and identify deviations that need review.

6
00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:39.540
A baseline should be maintained as systems evolve.

7
00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:47.000
It is not just a document created once and forgotten; it is a reference point that should stay aligned with operational and security needs.
